{
 "cells": [
  {
   "id": "cell-00",
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Kalman Filter Price-Target Model — Fused MvGRW Panel\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notebook form of `pymc_kalman_filter_pt.py`**, aligned with\n",
    "`probabilistic_ml_model/pymc_models/KalmanFilterModel.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cross-sectional spine is the **fused MvGRW panel model**\n",
    "(`build_fused_kalman_pt_model`):\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Model B spine** — a diagonal (NUTS-safe) Multivariate Gaussian Random Walk over the\n",
    "  `(isin, time, y_series)` response tensor with a cross-sectional baseline `mu_isin`.\n",
    "- **Model A refinement** — the volatility-aware `expected_return → risk_adj_return`\n",
    "  latent (with a non-centred logit-normal `achieve_prob`) *is* the GRW baseline\n",
    "  `mu_isin`, and the heteroscedastic scale `sigma_isin = sigma_base · (1 + cv) / √n`\n",
    "  replaces the cv-free form. The risk adjustment is keyed on **expected volatility**\n",
    "  (the `feat_vol_*` term-structure mean) rather than analyst conviction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The workflow has two halves:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Sections    | Scope                                                                                                                        |\n",
    "|-------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n",
    "| **§1–§10**  | Fused cross-sectional panel — one row per ISIN from `pml.mv_pymc_kalman_pt`                                                  |\n",
    "| **§11–§14** | Single-security / cohort time-series — the `KalmanFilterPriceTarget` GRW filter on the embedded `*_ago` price-target history |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Schema is the single source of truth (`pml` schema):** MV `pml.mv_pymc_kalman_pt`,\n",
    "catalogue `pml.vw_pymc_feature_catalogue WHERE model_target = 'kalman_pt'`, coords\n",
    "`pml.vw_pml_df_coords`.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Design note.** This notebook *orchestrates* the functions defined in\n",
    "> `pymc_kalman_filter_pt.py`; it does not re-implement them. The module stays the\n",
    "> single source of truth, and each section here calls into it and keeps the returned\n",
    "> artifact at the top level so you can inspect it interactively."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-01",
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §0 — Environment & imports\n",
    "\n",
    "`PYTENSOR_FLAGS` must be set **before** PyTensor/PyMC are first imported. On Windows\n",
    "the flag parser strips backslashes from the `cxx` path (`C:\\msys64\\...` →\n",
    "`C:msys64...`, a nonexistent compiler that hangs the *\"Compiling new CVM\"* step), so we\n",
    "emit the g++ path with **forward slashes**, which survive the parser. If you launched\n",
    "this kernel after `. .\\set_env.ps1`, the existing flag is respected; otherwise we\n",
    "auto-detect g++ and set a safe value here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-02",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:17.135006400Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:16.989635800Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set a parser-safe PYTENSOR_FLAGS *before* importing pymc/pytensor (idempotent).\n",
    "if \"cxx=\" not in os.environ.get(\"PYTENSOR_FLAGS\", \"\"):\n",
    "    _gxx = next(\n",
    "        (p for p in (r\"C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/g++.exe\", r\"C:/msys64/mingw64/bin/g++.exe\")\n",
    "         if Path(p).exists()),\n",
    "        \"\",  # empty cxx -> pure-Python / numba path (nutpie still works)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    os.environ[\"PYTENSOR_FLAGS\"] = f\"floatX=float64,cxx={_gxx}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "import pytensor\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"PyTensor\", pytensor.__version__, \"| cxx =\", repr(pytensor.config.cxx),\n",
    "      \"| exists:\", bool(pytensor.config.cxx) and Path(pytensor.config.cxx).exists())"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "PyTensor 3.0.7 | cxx = 'C:msys64ucrt64bing++.exe' | exists: False\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "C:\\Users\\markm\\PML_Finance_Project\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pytensor\\configparser.py:309: UserWarning: PyTensor does not recognise this flag: device\n",
      "  warnings.warn(f\"PyTensor does not recognise this flag: {key}\")\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-03",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:18.637156900Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:17.136005Z"
    }
   },
   "source": "import logging\n\nimport pymc as pm\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\n\n# Section functions live in the module (single source of truth) — import, don't re-define.\nimport pymc_kalman_filter_pt as kf\nfrom pymc_kalman_filter_pt import (\n    RANDOM_SEED,\n    setup_plotting, resolve_db_url,\n    load_kalman_df, load_feature_catalogue, resolve_feature_roles,\n    run_eda, map_state_space_features, prepare_kalman_panel_inputs,\n    build_panel_model, run_prior_predictive, sample_posterior, run_posterior_predictive,\n    run_diagnostics, summarize_panel_screen, export_analytics,\n    run_single_isin_filter, run_single_isin_stochastic_vol,\n    run_mingled_cohort_filter, run_mingled_cohort_stochastic_vol,\n    run_granular_forest, run_granular_further_views,\n    run_summary, run_recommendations,\n    present_group_effects,\n)\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=os.environ.get(\"LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\"))\nsetup_plotting()\nengine = create_engine(resolve_db_url())\nprint(\"Setup complete — RANDOM_SEED =\", RANDOM_SEED, \"| orchestrating:\", kf.__file__)",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Setup complete — RANDOM_SEED = 42 | orchestrating: C:\\Users\\markm\\PML_Finance_Project\\pymc_kalman_filter_pt.py\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-04",
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §1 — Data load & feature-role resolution\n",
    "\n",
    "- `load_kalman_df` — cross-sectional `pml.mv_pymc_kalman_pt` snapshot (one row per ISIN,\n",
    "  filtered to `observed_pt IS NOT NULL` and next earnings in the modelling horizon).\n",
    "- `load_feature_catalogue` — the `kalman_pt` rows of `pml.vw_pymc_feature_catalogue`.\n",
    "- `resolve_feature_roles` — groups columns by `pymc_role` (catalogue SSOT, MV-schema\n",
    "  fallback): predictors, coords, responses, classification coords, fiscal-calendar and\n",
    "  day-count columns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-05",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:19.134551400Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:18.679943500Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "kalman_df = load_kalman_df(engine)\n",
    "feature_catalogue = load_feature_catalogue(engine)\n",
    "roles = resolve_feature_roles(kalman_df, feature_catalogue)\n",
    "kalman_df.head()"
   ],
