  {
   "id": "cell-10",
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §4 — Fused-panel data containers\n",
    "\n",
    "`prepare_kalman_panel_inputs` filters to log-space-usable rows and builds the\n",
    "`KalmanPanelInputs`: the standardised `(isin, time, y_series)` response tensor `Y`, the\n",
    "fiscal-anchor time matrix `t_scaled`, the standardised drift design matrix, the\n",
    "volatility / dispersion-cv / √n noise drivers, and the categorical group-effect coords."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-11",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:26.641340200Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:26.546572700Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "panel = prepare_kalman_panel_inputs(kalman_df, roles, drift_features)\n",
    "print(\"Y shape (isin, time, y_series):\", panel.Y.shape)\n",
    "print(\"response_names:\", panel.response_names)\n",
    "print(\"drift_names   :\", panel.drift_names)"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Fused panel — isins:6227  T:1  D:3 (['feat_implied_upside', 'observed_pt', 'feat_pt_drift'])\n",
      "  drift_features:7  expected_vol(mean):45.597  cv(mean):0.199\n",
      "Y shape (isin, time, y_series): (6227, 1, 3)\n",
      "response_names: ['feat_implied_upside', 'observed_pt', 'feat_pt_drift']\n",
      "drift_names   : ['feat_pt_drift', 'feat_price_drift', 'feat_pt_high_drift', 'feat_pt_low_drift', 'feat_pt_median_drift', 'feat_coverage_drift', 'feat_total_return_ytd']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 6
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-12",
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §5 — Build the fused MvGRW model\n",
    "\n",
    "`build_panel_model` wraps `build_fused_kalman_pt_model` and renders the model graph.\n",
    "\n",
    "NUTS-inplace-safety constraints baked into the builder:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `√n_analysts` is precomputed in NumPy and passed as `pm.Data` (never `pt.sqrt` on an\n",
    "  integer container).\n",
    "- `sigma_base` uses `pm.Exponential` (not `HalfNormal`) so no `Abs→Sqrt` rewrite fuses\n",
    "  into an inplace `Composite` op.\n",
    "- The GRW uses an explicit **diagonal** innovation parameterisation instead of\n",
    "  `LKJCholeskyCov` (whose onion-method Beta→Normal chain triggers an inplace rewrite\n",
    "  NUTS rejects).\n",
    "\n",
    "Pass `robust=False` for the Normal-likelihood twin (default is the Student-t panel\n",
    "likelihood, which absorbs analyst outliers)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-13",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:28.948715700Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:26.976620700Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "robust = True\n",
    "model = build_panel_model(panel, robust=robust)\n",
    "pm.model_to_graphviz(model)"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
