   "source": [
    "## §6 — Prior predictive checks\n",
    "\n",
    "`run_prior_predictive` draws from the prior and overlays the prior implied-upside against\n",
    "the empirical `observed_pt / last_price − 1`, plus the logit-normal `achieve_prob` and\n",
    "heteroscedastic `sigma_isin` priors. The predictive sampling now forces the pure-Python\n",
    "linker via `compile_kwargs`, so it cannot stall on C compilation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-15",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T20:36:06.849981200Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:32:28.993722100Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "prior_idata = run_prior_predictive(model, panel)"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
