   "source": [
    "## §7 — Posterior inference (NUTS)\n",
    "\n",
    "`sample_posterior` tries `nutpie → numpyro → pymc` in priority order and merges the prior\n",
    "groups into the posterior for one-object downstream access.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Revised sampler settings** (see `sample_posterior`): `draws=1000, tune=1000, chains=4,\n",
    "cores=4, target_accept=0.95`. 4×1000 = 4000 draws gives ample ESS; `cores=4` runs all\n",
    "chains in parallel. `target_accept=0.95` is kept for the GRW funnel geometry.\n",
    "\n",
    "> This is the long-running cell. With the `cxx` path fixed, nutpie compiles via numba\n",
    "> (no g++ stall)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cell-17",
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-06-19T21:04:32.108020700Z",
     "start_time": "2026-06-19T20:36:06.913285300Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "idata = sample_posterior(model, prior_idata)\n",
    "print(\"Group effects fitted:\", present_group_effects(idata))\n",
    "idata.posterior"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
